// SimpleBleedoutKO 2.0.0 - THE SKIN-MARK TABLE: which Battle Wounds mark shows for which Injury Engine wound.
// Read ONCE when the game starts. Comments (//) are allowed. A row with a mistake is skipped with one log line.
//
// "files": a mark code -> its area (Face / Body / Hands / Feet), its default tint, and its textures relative to Data/Textures:
//          "U": [female, male] for one file, or "L": [female, male] + "R": [female, male] for a left / right pair (her own side).
//          Battle Wounds (its "Collygon - Wounds" folder) is installed by the player - it is not part of this mod. SlaveTats paths
//          get a leading backslash when painted, so SlaveTats never claims or blanks SBKO's slots. Every file is checked at start
//          (present, square, a power of two - a texture that is not is refused, as a wrong size can crash the game).
// "families": a look -> for each body part ("face", "back", "arm", "leg") the marks it shows, in order:
//          "code" (one) or "pick" (her stable pick among several - it never jumps between reads), "at" = the lowest IE stage it
//          shows at (light by default), "side": "other" = the other side, "tint" = override, "blood": true = one step lighter.
//          Face: the 1st entry = the base mark, the 2nd / 3rd = layers at medium / severe (bFaceLayers). Body: one mark per wounded
//          part, the worst parts first (Body 3-5 = three). Hands / Feet = SBKO's own wrist / ankle band (bWristAnkleBands).
// "sources": an Injury Engine source id -> its family (one, or one per stage light / medium / severe); "" = no art (unmarked);
//          "standin" = used only with bStandIns=1; "real": false = a torture wound (a real wound wins a tie on a part).
// Strength: light 0.50, medium 0.75, severe 1.00, floor 0.30 (sStageAlphas / fAlphaFloor / fAlphaScale in SimpleBleedoutKO.ini).
{
  "version": 1,
  "tints": { "C": "5A6EC8", "R": "FFFFFF", "K": "3C3028", "V": "8C78D0" },

